I agree with what John Clare says.

I would add that I don't think it's possible to work on community models without going down the Bayesian methods road simply because a species level random effect is probably called for.   You could subset to your common species and then fit joint models with species fixed effects, but that seems really unappealing from a community modeling perspective where the random effects structure is so natural.

